     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled metformin dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, if you want a lower or starting dose.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and add a note with your rationale. I'll enter it as you direct, though pharmacy will probably flag it."
      }
     ],
